; The launcher's OsUpdater drives update_engine through the root shell (phh su, domain
; phhsu_daemon). update_engine_client --follow binds a status callback, and update_engine was
; denied the call back into that domain on the bench unit (2026-10-07):
;
;   avc: denied { call } scontext=u:r:update_engine:s0 tcontext=u:r:phhsu_daemon:s0 tclass=binder
;   update_engine_client: Failed to bind() the UpdateEngine daemon.
;
; phhsu_daemon is declared in the GSI's system_ext_sepolicy.cil; CIL resolves it across files.
; Compiled against the 0.2 set with init's secilc flags: builds, and no neverallow line changes.
(allow update_engine phhsu_daemon (binder (call transfer)))
;
; The COW images of a Virtual A/B update live in /data; on this unit libfiemap maps them through
; a loop device, and update_engine was denied writing it (bench, 2026-10-07):
;
;   avc: denied { write } name="loop0" scontext=u:r:update_engine:s0 tcontext=u:object_r:loop_device:s0
;   update_engine: Can't zero-fill COW device for system_ext_a: /dev/block/loop0 (kInstallDeviceOpenError)
(allow update_engine loop_device (blk_file (open read write ioctl getattr)))
